ood questions so  g  blocks and the g blocks hi-fi gene  fragments are suitable for direct  transfection  um there's a few things to consider  though we do recommend filter  sterilization  with a 0.22 micron filter before use  some researchers have observed toxicity  in cells when you transfect large  amounts of double  double stranded dna that sensitivity  does vary  depending on which cell line you're  working on so we do suggest titrating  concentrations  of the double-stranded fragments just to  determine what that optimal delivery  will be  for your particular cell type  great thank you and our last question is  how many colony spots have you tried  spotting  on the sbs omni trays  that's a good question so we safely  transfer 1536 spot spots on  an lb agar plate that is a standard size  and like those omni trays you mentioned  but  it doesn't mean that if we push for it  we cannot go higher but 1536 is a safe  number  thank you again sahil and tom do you  have any final comments for our audience  before we go  i wanted to invite the audience to feel  free to reach out to us with any of  their simple to complex gene assembly  projects and let us be part of their  solution  yeah absolutely uh as sahela says you  know please do contact us with any  questions or if there's anything we can  do to help and i'd just like to say  thank you again to everybody for joining  us today  and to our host lavree and our sponsors  beckman call to life science  it's been a pleasure speaking to you  thank you  before we go i'd like to thank the  audience for joining us today and for  their questions  any questions we did not have time for  today and those submitted during the  on-demand period will be addressed by  the speaker  via the contact information you provided  at the time of registration  we would like to once again thank  sohaila and tom for their time today  and for their important research we  would also like to thank labrutz and our  sponsor beckman culture life sciences  for underwriting today's educational  webcast  this webcast can be viewed on demand lab  routes will alert you via email when  it's available for replay  we encourage you to share that email  with your colleagues who may have missed  today's live event  until next time goodbye
 

